<title>UK: McAlpine, CALA settle copyright feud.</title>
<headline>McAlpine, CALA settle copyright feud.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>British construction group Alfred McAlpine Plc and British housebuilding and commercial property developer CALA Plc said on Friday they had resolved a legal action concerning breach of design copyright.</p>
<p>The companies said under the agreement McAlpine was to pay CALA 1.85 million pounds. The payment will be taken as a one-off operating exceptional item in the 1996 accounts.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
